      'Katanga\'s secession under Moise Tshombe was propped up substantially by Union Minière du Haut Katanga and covert support from Belgium and other Western interests anxious to keep Katanga\'s mineral wealth out of a Congolese central government they distrusted. The resulting conflict drew in one of the largest and most fraught UN peacekeeping operations to that date (ONUC). Katanga\'s secession was ultimately ended by UN military action in January 1963.',
