      'The Nigerian federal government\'s blockade of secessionist Biafra caused mass starvation among Biafran civilians, producing globally circulated images of starving children that generated unprecedented international humanitarian attention. The federal government defended the blockade as a legitimate wartime measure to prevent arms smuggling and hasten the secession\'s end. Estimates of famine deaths, disproportionately affecting children, range widely, commonly cited at one to two million.',
